WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Campaigns tutorial: See what is working, and compare.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Page 1 of 3: Campaign Overview. Every platform’s results in one place.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.108
Campaign Overview shows the results each ad platform reports, in one place.

4
00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:18.036
Switch platform, campaign or date range; the metrics follow what that platform reports.

5
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:21.492
Metrics a platform doesn’t report show a dash, never an invented number.

6
00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:24.092
Page 2 of 3: Campaign Comparison. Campaigns side by side.

7
00:00:26.721 --> 00:00:32.295
Campaign Comparison puts campaigns side by side on the figures their platforms report.

8
00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:35.513
Anything a platform didn’t report shows as not reported, never as zero.

9
00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:39.568
Pinterest reports per ad account only, so its campaigns can’t be compared one by one.

10
00:00:39.568 --> 00:00:42.168
Page 3 of 3: Campaign Builder. Adjust a campaign before it is published.

11
00:00:44.763 --> 00:00:50.816
Campaign Builder opens from Campaign Overview and lists every campaign you created.

12
00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:54.033
Open one to work on it before it is published: here, a Google Search campaign.

13
00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:58.452
Ask for changes in plain words in the chat. (Typed here to show it; not sent.)

14
00:00:58.452 --> 00:01:04.607
The campaign details on the right show its budget, objective, keywords and ad text.
